# shadcn/ui (rudiment)

Interactive UI primitives come from **shadcn/ui** — not one-off styled `div`s for buttons, dialogs, forms, tables, sheets, or empty states. Shell chrome stays on **Tokens + surface boundaries + product icon registry**.

Official skill docs: https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/skills  
Install skill: `npx skills add shadcn/ui` → project `.cursor/skills/shadcn/` (and/or `.agents/skills/shadcn/`)

## Do

- Before inventing a control, load the **shadcn** skill and use `npx shadcn@latest search` / `docs` / `add`
- Compose pages from registry components (FieldGroup forms, Dialog/Sheet, Tabs, Table, Empty, Sonner, etc.)
- Use semantic shadcn colors (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`) **inside** shadcn components
- Keep product shell themed via Tokens (`t`)
- Register every new meaningful region with the surface-boundary wrapper
- Chrome / tree icons → product icon registry; control icons inside shadcn → lucide (per icons + shadcn rules)

## Don't

- Hand-roll Button / Dialog / Select / form layouts when shadcn already has them
- Override shadcn component colors with raw hex or one-off Tailwind color utilities
- Skip `components.json` — the skill activates fully when that file exists
- Replace product shell patterns with a generic shadcn Sidebar without an explicit decision
- Drop surface boundaries because a region uses shadcn primitives

## Adapt for this repo

- Point skill path at `.cursor/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md`
- Point Tokens + HolonBoundary at real paths once they exist
- Init under the app package that owns UI (e.g. `apps/<product>/`)

## Bootstrap

If `components.json` is missing and the task needs shadcn primitives, **init shadcn** in the UI package first, then add components. Align CSS variables with the product accent so shadcn and Tokens stay aligned.
